This is caused by two things (normally):

1.  You didn't install enough OSF-BASE licences to for DEC OSF to be happy
(when you attempt to telnet in, a console message should appear telling
you what it wants).

2.  You did install all the correct bases, but for some reason lmf
isn't resting the in-kernel license cache.  Type 'lmf reset' as root to
fix this.[1]


[1]  I have had two installed of Patchkit2 for 4.0d delete
/sbin/rc3.d/03startlmf for me.  It's not very reproduceable, though.





