1. Tru64 Unix System Administration Course.

We are pleased to announce the following one day course:

-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*
Tru64 Unix (formerly Digital Unix and OSF/1) System Administration
-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*

to be held on 25th May 1999 at:

CLRC Daresbury Laboratory
Daresbury
Warrington
Cheshire
WA4 4AD

The course is **FREE** to all EPSRC grant holders and associated UK
academics, and follows on from previous DisCo courses on AIX and Irix
system administration, which were both well received by attendees.

The following topics will be covered:

  Introduction to Tru64
  System Configuration
  Disks and Filesystems
  Managing Users
  Networking
  Software Installation and Maintenance
  Software Licensing
  The X-Windows Environment & CDE
  System Tuning
  System Security

Who Should Attend?

 * Anyone who looks after Tru64 (Digital Unix) systems and has
   responsibility for all aspects of the effective running of
   those systems.
 * The course will be aimed at both those who are managing Tru64 Unix
   system for the first time, and those coming from other Unix
   environments.
 * The course will cover topics common to several implementations of
   the Unix Operating System, and will be presented to give a complete
   picture of those services that work similarly across Unix OS's.

You can register for the course in many ways:

